{"agent":"bgf","data":{"by":"bgf","evidence":{"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"note":"Claim CONFIRMED: the shipped help page ddflow/templates/prompts/help/workflow.md said of --needs 'An id that does not exist is treated as UNMET, deliberately', but the ADD path refuses unknown needs. Probe: ddflow/services/items.py unknown_needs() returns 'no such id {need!r}. Add it first, or fix the typo.' (line ~201) and is called from api/items/_add.py _edges_problem (allow_unknown_needs=False for task add). usage: ddflow update [-h] [--title TITLE] [--body BODY]\n                     [--append-body APPEND_BODY] [--needs NEEDS]\n                     [--add-needs ADD_NEEDS] [--remove-needs REMOVE_NEEDS]\n                     [--allow-unknown-needs] [--tags TAGS]\n                     [--add-tags ADD_TAGS] [--remove-tags REMOVE_TAGS]\n                     [--line LINE] [--resources RESOURCES] [--globs GLOBS]\n                     [--add-globs ADD_GLOBS] [--remove-globs REMOVE_GLOBS]\n                     [--priority PRIORITY] [--queue] [--landed LANDED]\n                     [--landed-paths LANDED_PATHS] [--parent PARENT]\n                     [--phase PHASE] [--kind KIND] [--worktree WORKTREE]\n                     id\n\npositional arguments:\n  id\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --title TITLE\n  --body BODY\n  --append-body APPEND_BODY\n                        ADD this text after the item's current body; the\n                        original is kept\n  --needs NEEDS\n  --add-needs ADD_NEEDS\n                        ADD these comma-separated ids to the item's needs; the\n                        rest are kept\n  --remove-needs REMOVE_NEEDS\n                        REMOVE these comma-separated ids from the item's needs\n  --allow-unknown-needs\n                        accept needs that name an id not in the queue (one\n                        that will exist later, or `repo:ID`)\n  --tags TAGS\n  --add-tags ADD_TAGS   ADD these comma-separated tags to the item's tags; the\n                        rest are kept\n  --remove-tags REMOVE_TAGS\n                        REMOVE these comma-separated tags from the item's tags\n  --line LINE\n  --resources RESOURCES\n  --globs GLOBS         REPLACES the item's globs (and a claimed item's lease)\n                        with these -- the whole list, not an addition (see\n                        --add-globs); an empty value means none, and a fix\n                        task then takes none from its bug; path globs, comma-\n                        separated (a.py,src/**) or a JSON array; repeat the\n                        flag to add more -- every value is kept\n  --add-globs ADD_GLOBS\n                        ADD these comma-separated globs to the item's current\n                        ones (and a claimed item's lease); the rest are kept\n  --remove-globs REMOVE_GLOBS\n                        REMOVE these comma-separated globs from the item's\n                        current ones (and a claimed item's lease)\n  --priority PRIORITY\n  --queue               keep a refused --globs widening in the first-in-first-\n                        out line for its files\n  --landed LANDED       record the commit (or <before>..<after>) on the base\n                        that holds this item's work merged outside `ddflow\n                        merge`; refused unless it is on the base and touches\n                        the item's globs\n  --landed-paths LANDED_PATHS\n                        restrict the recorded landing to the item's own paths\n                        (comma-separated globs, verified inside the item's\n                        declared globs and the landing's changed files), so a\n                        commit that also changed code does not force the code\n                        pipeline on a docs-only item\n  --parent PARENT       move the task under this phase or task ('' = top\n                        level)\n  --phase PHASE         same as --parent\n  --kind KIND           change the work kind: task, doc, research or job (the\n                        gate pipeline [gates].kind_pipelines gives it)\n  --worktree WORKTREE   rebind the item (and your live lease on it) to this\n                        linked worktree and the branch checked out there --\n                        the way out of a binding to the wrong tree shows --needs/--add-needs and the explicit --allow-unknown-needs escape. So the page documented a behaviour the add path no longer has; only import keeps a dangling need as unmet.","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/templates/prompts/help/workflow.md":"100644 856a257cd6391da62ad51452f77e21d8dae8838f","tests/test_help.py":"100644 4ab8c08474f7849f7265b2c2d8ad2018f9e639e2"},"tree_sha":"04b06e78c68f+clean"},"gate":"research","reason":""},"id":"ed499c1c38a84a5ed50cb5724","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":159684,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B8b9fc41f60","ts":"2026-11-09T05:33:45.107719Z"}
